art:artigo_bunescu_acl07_trabalho_futuro_1 a art:TrabalhoFuturo ;
    art:extraidoDe art:artigo_bunescu_acl07_secao_9 ;
    art:pontuacao 7 ;
    art:texto "An interesting potential application of our approach is a web relation-extraction system similar to Google Sets, in which the user provides only a handful of pairs of entities known to exhibit or not to exhibit a particular relation, and the system is used to find other pairs of entities exhibiting the same relation."@en .

art:artigo_bunescu_acl07_trabalho_futuro_2 a art:TrabalhoFuturo ;
    art:extraidoDe art:artigo_bunescu_acl07_secao_9 ;
    art:pontuacao 7 ;
    art:texto "We are also investigating methods for reducing Type II bias, either by modifying the word weights, or by integrating an appropriate measure of word distribution across positive bags directly in the objective function for the MIL problem."@en .

art:artigo_dyer12_metodo_1 a art:Metodo ;
    art:extraidoDe art:artigo_dyer12_secao_1 ;
    art:pontuacao 5 ;
    art:texto "We deploy local features for SCFG-based SMT that can be read off from rules at runtime, and present a learning algorithm that applies l1/l2 regularization for joint feature selection over distributed stochastic learning processes."@en .

art:artigo_dyer12_metodo_2 a art:Metodo ;
    art:extraidoDe art:artigo_dyer12_secao_2 ;
    art:pontuacao 5 ;
    art:texto "We deploy generic features for SCFG-based SMT that can efficiently be read off from rules at runtime."@en .

art:artigo_dyer12_metodo_3 a art:Metodo ;
    art:extraidoDe art:artigo_dyer12_secao_2 ;
    art:pontuacao 5 ;
    art:texto "Another crucial ingredient of our approach is a combination of parallelized stochastic learning with feature selection inspired by multi-task learning."@en .

art:artigo_dyer12_objetivo_1 a art:Objetivo ;
    art:extraidoDe art:artigo_dyer12_secao_1 ;
    art:pontuacao 4 ;
    art:texto "The goal of this paper is to show that this common wisdom can also be brought to bear upon SMT."@en .

art:artigo_dyer12_objetivo_2 a art:Objetivo ;
    art:extraidoDe art:artigo_dyer12_secao_1 ;
    art:pontuacao 5 ;
    art:texto "We present experiments on learning on 1.5 million training sentences, and show significant improvements over tuning discriminative models on small development sets."@en .

art:artigo_dyer12_problema_1 a art:Problema ;
    art:extraidoDe art:artigo_dyer12_secao_2 ;
    art:pontuacao 4 ;
    art:texto "Features may be lexicalized and sparse, non-local and overlapping, or be designed to generalize beyond surface statistics by incorporating part-of-speech or syntactic labels."@en .

art:artigo_dyer12_problema_2 a art:Problema ;
    art:extraidoDe art:artigo_dyer12_secao_2 ;
    art:pontuacao 6 ;
    art:texto "Another possible reason why large training data did not yet show the expected improvements in discriminative SMT is a special overfitting problem of current popular online learning techniques."@en .

