art:artigo_roark13_metodo_1 a art:Metodo ;
    art:extraidoDe art:artigo_roark13_secao_1 ;
    art:pontuacao 6 ;
    art:texto "We present a word tagging approach using conditional random fields (CRFs) that allows a diversity of features to be considered during inference, including some capturing acoustic confusions encoded in word confusion networks."@en .

art:artigo_roark13_metodo_2 a art:Metodo ;
    art:extraidoDe art:artigo_roark13_secao_1 ;
    art:pontuacao 6 ;
    art:texto "We evaluate the approach under several scenarios, including both supervised and unsupervised training, the latter achieved by training on the output of a baseline automatic word-alignment model."@en .

art:artigo_roark13_metodo_3 a art:Metodo ;
    art:extraidoDe art:artigo_roark13_secao_2 ;
    art:pontuacao 4 ;
    art:texto "The approach is general enough to allow tagging of word confusion networks derived from lattices, thus allowing us to explore the utility of such representations to achieve robustness."@en .

art:artigo_roark13_objetivo_1 a art:Objetivo ;
    art:extraidoDe art:artigo_roark13_secao_2 ;
    art:pontuacao 5 ;
    art:texto "In this paper, we present and evaluate the use of word tagging models for this task, in contrast to just using automatic (unsupervised) word-alignment methods."@en .

art:artigo_roark13_objetivo_2 a art:Objetivo ;
    art:extraidoDe art:artigo_roark13_secao_2 ;
    art:pontuacao 5 ;
    art:texto "We present results under a range of experimental conditions, including: variously adapting the ASR models to the domain; using maximum entropy models rather than CRFs; differing tagsets (BIO versus IO); and with varying degrees of supervision."@en .

art:artigo_roark13_problema_1 a art:Problema ;
    art:extraidoDe art:artigo_roark13_secao_1 ;
    art:pontuacao 4 ;
    art:texto "Automatically assessing the fidelity of a retelling to the original narrative - a task of growing clinical importance - is challenging, given extensive paraphrasing during retelling along with cascading automatic speech recognition (ASR) errors."@en .

art:artigo_roark13_problema_2 a art:Problema ;
    art:extraidoDe art:artigo_roark13_secao_7 ;
    art:pontuacao 5 ;
    art:texto "Although this presents a challenge for ASR, part of the goal of our work is to demonstrate the robustness of our methods to noisy audio."@en .

